causal"],"segregation":"mutant allele putatively inherited from each parent","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["A 22-year-old man (FC355; Fig. 1b, III-2) was the second child of healthy non-consanguineous parents.","At age 13, he first felt gait and balance problems.","Bilateral flat feet, and atrophic changes of intrinsic hand, foot and calf muscles were also noted (Fig. 2d)."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"},{"id":"R:30298599:1","pmid":"30298599","label":"Family 1","kind":"family","family":"Family 1","n_affected":null,"n_families":1,"sex":"","ancestry":"","consanguinity":"not_stated","onset":"","age_last":"","phenotypes":[{"text":"sensorimotor axonal neuropathy","hpo_label":"Sensorimotor neuropathy","hpo_id":"HP:0007141","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"hepatocerebral involvement","hpo_label":"Abnormality of the liver","hpo_id":"HP:0001392","present":false,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"MPV17","as_reported":"c.122G>A (p.Arg41Gln)","cdna":"c.122G>A","protein":"p.Arg41Gln","genomic":"","zygosity":"homozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"missense","key":"V2"}],"variant_roles":["causal"],"segregation":"","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["Here, we describe five additional patients from two unrelated families with sensorimotor axonal neuropathy without hepatocerebral affection caused by homozygous MPV17 variants.","Patients of the first family carried the known c.122G>A variant"],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"},{"id":"R:30298599:2","pmid":"30298599","label":"Family 2","kind":"family","family":"Family 2","n_affected":null,"n_families":1,"sex":"","ancestry":"","consanguinity":"not_stated","onset":"","age_last":"","phenotypes":[{"text":"sensorimotor axonal neuropathy","hpo_label":"Sensorimotor neuropathy","hpo_id":"HP:0007141","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"hepatocerebral involvement","hpo_label":"Abnormality of the liver","hpo_id":"HP:0001392","present":false,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"MPV17","as_reported":"c.376-9T>G","cdna":"c.376-9T>G","protein":"","genomic":"","zygosity":"homozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"splice site (in-frame deletion of 11 amino acids)","key":"V3"}],"variant_roles":["causal"],"segregation":"","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["affected individuals of the second family had a novel c.376-9T>G near-splice variant, which was shown to result in an in-frame deletion of 11 amino acids.","Here, we describe five additional patients from two unrelated families with sensorimotor axonal neuropathy without hepatocerebral affection caused by homozygous MPV17 variants."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"}],"notes":[{"id":"N:30298599:1","pmid":"30298599","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Baumann et al. (2019) found that the novel MPV17 c.376-9T>G near-splice variant resulted in an in-frame deletion of 11 amino acids.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["a novel c.376-9T>G near-splice variant, which was shown to result in an in-frame deletion of 11 amino acids"],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:30298599:2","pmid":"30298599","section":"diagnosis","statement":"Baumann et al. (2019) concluded that MPV17 mutations should be considered in patients with pure, non-syndromic axonal neuropathy of juvenile or adult onset.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["This report provides further evidence that MPV17 mutations should be considered in patients with pure, non-syndromic axonal neuropathy."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:26437932:1","pmid":"26437932","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"In 2 patients from unrelated Korean families with axonal sensorimotor polyneuropathy without liver or brain involvement, Choi et al. (2015) identified a homozygous c.122G-A (p.R41Q) mutation in MPV17 by whole-exome sequencing. The mutation was not found in 300 controls or in-house exome data, and was present at very low frequency in ESP and ExAC.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["a novel homozygous mutation c.122G> A (p.R41Q) in MPV17 was identified in both families (Fig. 1b). A mutant allele was putatively inherited from each parent in both families. The mutation was not observed in the 300 controls and in-house exome data (n = 302)."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:26437932:2","pmid":"26437932","section":"gene_function","statement":"Choi et al. (2015) found that knockdown of MPV17 in NSC34 mouse motor neuronal cells significantly reduced cell proliferation and viability against reactive oxygen species and affected OXPHOS levels, and that overexpression of the p.R41Q mutant significantly inhibited cell proliferation, suggesting both loss of function and detrimental effects of the mutant protein.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["knockdown of MPV17 significantly reduced the cell proliferation (Fig. 5b) and viability against ROS in mouse motor neuronal cells (Fig. 5c).","Expression of p.R41Q mutant protein significantly inhibited cell proliferation when compared to controls (Fig. 5e)."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:26437932:3","pmid":"26437932","section":"clinical_features","statement":"Choi et al. (2015) noted that both patients had sensory nerve action potentials absent from early disease, absent peroneal and tibial CMAPs, and lower leg MRI showing selective fatty infiltration of the soleus muscle, similar to CMT2A, consistent with length-dependent axonal degeneration.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["Sensory-nerve action potentials of the sural nerve were lost in the early stage of the disease.","the lower leg MRIs exhibit selective fatty infiltration with a preference for soleus muscles, similar to CMT type 2A (CMT2A) caused by MFN2 mutations."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:22508010:1","pmid":"22508010","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"In a 21-year-old Pakistani man with adult-onset axonal sensorimotor polyneuropathy, leukoencephalopathy, and mild liver involvement, Blakely et al. (2012) identified a homozygous missense mutation (P98L) in the MPV17 gene. Muscle showed multiple mtDNA deletions with normal mtDNA copy number, a finding not previously noted in patients with MPV17 mutations.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["Long-range PCR amplification showed the presence of multiple mtDNA deletions (Fig. 3a), confirming a disorder of mtDNA maintenance.","we identified multiple mtDNA deletions in skeletal muscle, a finding not previously noted in patients with MPV17 mutations."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:22508010:2","pmid":"22508010","section":"pathogenesis","statement":"Blakely et al. (2012) found that single laser-captured COX-deficient muscle fibers from the patient had high levels of clonally expanded mtDNA deletions involving MTND4 without mtDNA copy number abnormality, and concluded that MPV17 is involved in both mtDNA replication and repair, associated with both quantitative and qualitative mtDNA abnormalities.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["Real-time PCR of individual, laser-captured COX-deficient fibres also failed to identify a mtDNA copy number abnormality but clearly revealed that a proportion of fibres had high levels of clonally-expanded mtDNA deletion involving the MTND4 gene","we confirm this protein as being intimately involved in both the mtDNA replication and repair processes and associated with both quantitative and qualitative mtDNA abnormalities."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:22508010:3","pmid":"22508010","section":"clinical_features","statement":"Blakely et al. (2012) noted that the phenotype of their patient was similar to the classic form of Navajo neurohepatopathy but unusual in showing muscle involvement with ragged-red fibers and mosaic COX deficiency.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["The case we present, although phenotypically similar to the classic form of NNH, is unusual in several respects. Importantly, histochemical analysis demonstrated clear evidence of muscle involvement with ragged red fibres and a mosaic pattern of COX deficiency."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]}],"dropped":{"records":[],"notes":[]},"gene_decisions":{"candidates":["MPV17"],"confirmed":["MPV17"],"dropped":[],"not_confirmed":[]},"candidate_inheritance":["AR"]}